<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9534] Wrong error message in bin/include/functions.sh</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9534</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In the case when we don&apos;t have java installed on the host I see a&#160;message:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
echo $0&quot;, ERROR:&quot;

&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; echo &quot;JAVA_HOME environment variable is not found.&quot;

&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; echo &quot;Please point JAVA_HOME variable to location of JDK 1.7 or JDK 1.8.&quot;

&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; echo &quot;You can also download latest JDK at http://java.com/download&quot;

&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Java versions should be changed to:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;
&#160;JDK 1.8 or JDK 9

&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
